==English==

===Etymology===
From the French Imperial forename ''[[Napoleon]]'', usually with reference to [[w:Napoleon Bonaparte|Napoleon Bonaparte]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/nə'pəʊlɪən/}}
*: {{rhymes|əʊliən}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# a gold [[coin]] worth twenty [[franc]]s issued by Napoleon I; a twenty-franc coin
#:* '''1891''': We had occasion some months ago to strengthen our resources, and borrowed, for that purpose, thirty thousand '''napoleons''' from the Bank of France. — Arthur Conan Doyle, ‘The Red-Headed League’ (Norton 2005 p.67)

==Other uses==
* The main antagonist of [[Wikipedia:George Orwell|George Orwell]]'s novel ''[[Wikipedia:Animal Farm|Animal Farm]]''.
* [[Wikipedia:Professor Moriarty|Professor Moriarty]] - The arch-enemy of Sherlock Holmes, sometimes referred to as "the Napoleon of Crime."
* [[Wikipedia:Napoleon complex|Napoleon complex]] - A psychological condition in which a person of diminutive stature attempts to compensate for their lack of height by being aggressive toward people taller than themselves.

